```

## Tutorials

A prime number is only divisible by 1 and itself.

To test if a number is prime, we try dividing it by every number from 2 up to its square root:

Explanation:We start with the number29. Since 29 is greater than 1, the loop checks if it can be divided evenly by any number from 2 up to the square root of 29 (about 5.38). The numbers 2, 3, 4, and 5 do not divide 29 without a remainder, so the program concludes that29is prime.

### Code Examples

```
Example
int n = 29;  // Number used to check
boolean isPrime = n > 1;

for (int i = 2; i * i <= n; i++) {
  if (n % i == 0) {
    isPrime = false;
    break;
  }
}

System.out.println(n + (isPrime ? " is prime" : " is not prime"));
Try it Yourself »
```

